Every Aura you CAST pulls a second one out of your library for free. Light-Paws searches for an Aura with mana value no greater than the one you cast and a name you don't already have, and puts it straight onto her. So a two-mana Aura is really two Auras, and a four-mana one can fetch the best four-drop in the deck. Stack protection first, then damage, then swing with a commander nobody can touch.

# The commander
Light-Paws, Emperor's Voice :: two mana. Whenever an Aura you control enters, if you CAST it, search for an Aura with mana value less than or equal to it and a different name from every Aura you control, and put it onto the battlefield attached to Light-Paws. The fetched Aura was not cast, so it does not trigger her again: one cast, one fetch.
The cast Aura can go anywhere. Cast Reprobation on an opponent's creature and the fetch still lands on Light-Paws. But the FETCHED Aura always goes on her, so never fetch Reprobation, Darksteel Mutation or Swift Reconfiguration: they would shut her off. On Thin Ice cannot be fetched at all; it can only enchant a snow land.
Benevolent Blessing and Flickering Ward give protection from a colour you choose. Never choose white: protection from white stops your own new Auras attaching to her.

# Aura chains — what to cast, and what it fetches
Cast the most expensive Aura you can, because it sets the ceiling on the fetch.
Angelic Destiny -> Sage's Reverie :: four into four. Destiny makes her a 6/6 flying first-striker, then Reverie draws a card for every Aura on a creature and pumps her again. With three or more Auras out, this is the best card-draw turn in the deck.
Sage's Reverie -> Angelic Destiny :: the same pair the other way round, when Reverie is the one in hand.
Battle Mastery -> Chains of Custody :: double strike now, and the fetched Chains exiles an opponent's best nonland permanent until it leaves. Removal without spending a card.
Chains of Custody -> Battle Mastery :: cast Chains for the removal, fetch double strike onto her.
Twinblade Blessing -> Timely Ward :: Twinblade has flash, so cast it in their end step or mid-combat, and fetch indestructible in response to nothing at all.
Mantle of the Ancients -> Angelic Destiny :: Mantle returns every Aura and Equipment from your graveyard onto her, then fetches a four-drop. The rebuild after a wipe.
Reprobation -> Ethereal Armor :: cast the removal Aura on THEIR creature; the fetch still goes on Light-Paws.
Ethereal Armor -> Hyena Umbra :: the turn-two chain. First strike, plus umbra armor so the first removal spell misses.

# Making her lethal
Battle Mastery :: double strike. Every pump after this counts twice.
Twinblade Blessing :: double strike with flash: the surprise version.
Ethereal Armor :: +1/+1 for each enchantment you control, and first strike. With six Auras out it is +6/+6 on its own.
All That Glitters :: +1/+1 for each artifact and enchantment you control.
Daybreak Coronet :: needs another Aura already on her: +3/+3, first strike, vigilance and lifelink.
Idolized :: when she attacks alone, +X/+X where X is your nonland permanents.
Angelic Destiny :: +4/+4, flying and first strike, and it returns to your hand if she dies.
Kor Spiritdancer :: the backup body: +2/+2 per Aura on IT, and a card every time you cast an Aura.
Stoneskin + Solid Footing + Triclopean Sight :: Stoneskin gives +0/+10, Triclopean Sight gives vigilance, and Solid Footing makes a vigilant creature deal combat damage equal to its TOUGHNESS. With all three she is a 4/14 that hits for 14, or 28 with double strike.
Rogue's Passage :: {4}, {T}: she can't be blocked this turn.
Skrelv, Defector Mite :: gives her toxic 1 and makes her unblockable by a chosen colour; each hit is also poison.

# Keeping her alive
Mother of Runes :: protection from a colour at instant speed. Pick a colour that is NOT white if she is the target, or her Auras fall off.
Giver of Runes :: the same, from colourless too.
Swiftfoot Boots :: hexproof stops opponents only, so your own Auras still attach.
Brilliant Wings :: flash, flying and hexproof.
Shardmage's Rescue :: flash hexproof for the turn it enters. Cast it in response to removal; the fetch is a second Aura on top.
Timely Ward :: indestructible, castable at instant speed because it targets your commander.
Spirit Mantle :: protection from creatures: unblockable by creatures and immune to their abilities.
Unquestioned Authority :: protection from creatures, and it draws a card.
Mask of Law and Grace :: protection from black and red.
Shield of Duty and Reason :: protection from green and blue.
Benevolent Blessing :: flash protection from the chosen colour, never white.
Flickering Ward :: protection from a colour, and {W} returns it to hand to recast for another fetch.
Hyena Umbra :: umbra armor: the first destroy effect removes the Umbra instead of her.
Loran's Escape :: one mana, hexproof and indestructible for the turn.
Rebuff the Wicked :: counters a spell that targets your permanent.
Galadriel's Dismissal :: phase her out in response to removal, or kick it to phase out a blocker's whole board.
Teferi's Protection :: the reset button. Everything phases out, Auras included, and comes back attached.
Plaza of Heroes :: exile it for hexproof and indestructible on her.
Eiganjo Castle :: prevents 2 damage to a legendary creature each turn.
Pariah :: all damage to you is dealt to her instead. On a Light-Paws with Stoneskin or Timely Ward, nobody can hurt you.

# Removal that is also an Aura
Every one of these is a cast Aura, so each also fetches something onto Light-Paws.
Chains of Custody :: exiles a nonland permanent until Chains leaves, and gives her ward {2}.
Sheltered by Ghosts :: the same exile, plus lifelink and ward {2}.
Reprobation :: their creature becomes a 0/1 with no abilities.
Darksteel Mutation :: their creature becomes a 0/1 indestructible artifact with no abilities: good against creatures that come back.
Swift Reconfiguration :: turns a creature into a Vehicle that needs crew 5. Flash.
On Thin Ice :: exiles a creature. It enchants one of your snow lands, which is why the basics are Snow-Covered Plains.
Swords to Plowshares :: one mana, exile a creature.
Path to Exile :: the same, for a basic land.
Generous Gift :: destroys any permanent, for a 3/3 Elephant.

# Cards and mana
Sram, Senior Edificer :: draws on every Aura or Equipment you cast.
Mesa Enchantress :: draws on every enchantment you cast.
Pearl-Ear, Imperial Advisor :: enchantment spells cost {1} less for each Aura you control, and an Aura you cast on an enchanted Light-Paws draws a card.
Esper Sentinel :: taxes their first noncreature spell each turn.
Feather of Flight :: flash flying, and draws a card.
Serra's Sanctum :: taps for {W} per enchantment you control. With five Auras out it is five mana from a land.
Nykthos, Shrine to Nyx :: {2}, {T}: white mana equal to your devotion. Every Aura's {W} counts.
Land Tax :: three basics a turn when an opponent has more lands.
Archaeomancer's Map :: two Plains to hand, then lands when opponents get ahead.
Pearl Medallion :: white spells cost {1} less.
Sol Ring :: the usual.
Arcane Signet :: the usual.
Mind Stone :: a rock that cashes in for a card later.
Lotus Petal :: a free white for a turn-one Light-Paws.
Mox Amber :: taps for white once Light-Paws or another legend is out.
Urza's Saga :: chapter III fetches Sol Ring, Mox Amber or Lotus Petal.

# Locking the table
Grand Abolisher :: on your turn nobody can respond to the attack or the Aura chain.
Silence :: the one-turn version, cast before the big chain.
Archon of Emeria :: one spell per turn for everyone. Light-Paws is the least affected: one Aura a turn is still two.
Aven Mindcensor :: their searches only see the top four cards.
Hushbringer :: stops creature enter and death triggers. Your Auras' triggers are not creatures, so they still work.

# Getting it back
Replenish :: every enchantment in your graveyard returns at once. Auras that can't attach to anything stay behind.
Retether :: every Aura in your graveyard returns attached to creatures.
Mantle of the Ancients :: returns Auras and Equipment onto the creature it enchants.
Hall of Heliod's Generosity :: puts an enchantment from your graveyard on top of your library.
Gryff's Boon :: comes back from the graveyard for {3}{W}.
Sentinel's Eyes :: escapes from the graveyard for {W}.

# Tutor lines — what to fetch, and when
Open the Armory -> Battle Mastery :: any Aura to hand. Take Battle Mastery when she is already protected, a protection Aura when she is not.
Enlightened Tutor -> Angelic Destiny :: puts any enchantment on top of your library. Take the biggest Aura you can cast next turn, because it fetches the biggest second Aura.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep Light-Paws mana, one cheap Aura and one way to protect her. A hand of four-mana Auras with no early play is a mulligan.
Turn two Light-Paws, turn three cast a one-mana Aura to fetch Hyena Umbra or Shardmage's Rescue, then a damage Aura. Protection first, then damage.
Before the big chain, play Grand Abolisher or Silence so nobody can respond.
If she dies, Angelic Destiny comes back to your hand and Mantle of the Ancients or Retether rebuild the stack in one card.
